WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.959
What does this error mean, and how do I figure it out on my own?

2
00:00:04.959 --> 00:00:08.526
In this mission, you break a function on purpose.

3
00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:09.836
Look at this code.

4
00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:13.475
It asks for a field called nome, which means name.

5
00:00:13.475 --> 00:00:14.931
Now write this down:

6
00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:17.770
what happens if it gets an empty event?

7
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.318
And what status code do you expect?

8
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:25.270
Download the mission's two files and run this command.

9
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.968
You only need Python, no AWS account.

10
00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.280
An error shows up:

11
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.978
KeyError, and the name of the field.

12
00:00:31.978 --> 00:00:37.738
In other words, the code looked for the field called nome, and it wasn't there.

13
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.377
Now use AI as a tutor.

14
00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:43.892
Paste this request, with the code and the error.

15
00:00:43.892 --> 00:00:44.404
Notice:

16
00:00:44.404 --> 00:00:46.967
you ask it not to give you the fix.

17
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:50.335
It points to the line and asks you a question.

18
00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:53.776
Once you understand the cause, fix it yourself.

19
00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:57.656
What should the function do when the name is missing?

20
00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:03.215
If you already have an account, create the function on AWS.

21
00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:05.601
The commands are in the mission.

22
00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:08.062
Then call it with an empty event.

23
00:01:08.062 --> 00:01:10.970
This was the real response in our test.

24
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.387
Look at the detail.

25
00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:14.176
StatusCode 200.

26
00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:15.444
Right next to it:

27
00:01:15.444 --> 00:01:17.383
FunctionError, Unhandled.

28
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:18.874
And inside the file:

29
00:01:18.874 --> 00:01:19.620
KeyError.

30
00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:22.966
That's the point of this mission.

31
00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:26.994
The status is 200, and the function still failed.

32
00:01:26.994 --> 00:01:31.165
The 200 says the call to the Lambda service worked.

33
00:01:31.165 --> 00:01:34.204
Your function's error is in FunctionError.

34
00:01:34.204 --> 00:01:38.657
If you only look at the status, you think everything went fine.

35
00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:42.903
Wait about 15 seconds and read the log.

36
00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:45.330
It shows the error and line 5.

37
00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.934
Now ask your AI, without showing it this mission:

38
00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:54.597
if the StatusCode came back 200, did my function run without errors?

39
00:01:54.597 --> 00:01:56.510
Ask for the documentation.

40
00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.643
Did it notice the difference?

41
00:01:58.643 --> 00:02:00.481
Does the link confirm it?

42
00:02:00.481 --> 00:02:02.394
Open it and write it down.

43
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.903
At the end, clean up.

44
00:02:04.903 --> 00:02:10.630
The mission has the commands to delete the function, the role and the log group.

45
00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.565
The last line has to show empty brackets.

46
00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:16.428
That means the function is off the list.

47
00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:18.146
Then write your article:

48
00:02:18.146 --> 00:02:21.653
my Lambda returned 200 and it was broken.

49
00:02:21.653 --> 00:02:22.799
AI only reviews.

50
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.715
One note before we finish.

51
00:02:25.715 --> 00:02:31.828
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned voice, with my authorization.

52
00:02:31.828 --> 00:02:34.405
And this is an independent project.

53
00:02:34.405 --> 00:02:36.909
It is not official AWS material.
